{{Short description|none}}
Wrestlers from the [[United States]] have taken part in most of the major men's [[freestyle wrestling]] competitions over the years, in particular the [[Summer Olympic Games|Olympic Games]] and [[FILA Wrestling World Championships|World Wrestling Championships]]. Men's freestyle wrestling competition at the Olympics was first held in 1904. [[International Federation of Associated Wrestling Styles|FILA]] (now known as United World Wrestling) began holding World Championships in men's freestyle in 1951. 

During Olympic years there is only six weight classes contested, with the World Championships featuring ten weight classes since 2018. The World Championships contest the six Olympic, along with four non-Olympic weight classes. The United States did not send wrestlers to the championships in [[1951 FILA Wrestling World Championships|1951]], [[1957 FILA Wrestling World Championships|1957]], [[1959 FILA Wrestling World Championships|1959]], [[Wrestling at the 1980 Summer Olympics|1980]], and [[2002 FILA Wrestling World Championships|2002]]. No official team standings are kept for the Olympics. Some team finishes are approximate.

